<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Summary of Results for Different Values of <math id="S5.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">First, we evaluate the effect of the guidance weight <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> on the
performance of our model (Table 1). We do this by testing <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> from 0 to 11
and evaluating the Vina score. We report two different metrics: the first is the entire set of generated molecules, and
the second is
a ”filtered” list where we only take molecules of QED at least 0.40
and SAS at least 0.33. We find that <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=5</annotation></semantics></math> performs the best in terms of
Vina score and top 10% for the overall set of molecules. Note that the
filtered metrics have large uncertainty due to small sample size, so we choose
to rely more on the overall Vina metrics. Therefore, we use <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=5</annotation></semantics></math> for all remaining
experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S5.T2.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vina (<math id="S5.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vina (Top-10%) (<math id="S5.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></th>
